preConditionHook:
// EL: avgRange = average(h - l, rangeLookback)[lag + 1] -- the mean bar
// range over the rangeLookback bars ending at bar lag+1, so the outside bar
// itself is not in its own benchmark. Average recomputes from scratch every
// bar (EL_Summation_Probe, 2,808/2,808), so this is a FRESH loop and NOT the
// WFSafe_AvgTrueRange rolling accumulator. h - l is a price expression
// with real history, not an EL variable, so the loop reads price directly --
// contrast BarRangeAboveStd, which has to mirror a variable's zero-filled
// warm-up. Summed newest-first, EL's Summation order. Indexing the function
// result by a bar offset follows CloseAbovePriorHighestHigh's reading: the
// same statistic over the window shifted back by that many bars.
avgRange = 0.0;
for (int i = 0; i < (int)rangeLookback; ++i) {
    avgRange += high[(int)lag + 1 + i] - low[(int)lag + 1 + i];
}
avgRange /= (int)rangeLookback;
